"""D09 expected-outcome oracle generator (worker_02, finite code executor).

Builds the independent R4-D09 v0.5 expected-outcome oracle: per-case
expected_leaf_set / expected_source_leaf_set / expected_trace_leaf_set that
exist ONLY in this artifact (the catalog expected_* fields stay literal null).

Independence contract (execution context + contract §16):
  * This module NEVER reads the typed catalog, the challenge registry, the
    quota manifest, or any runtime code. All input facts come from the
    embedded explicit case/family specification table below (ORACLE_CASES),
    an independent copy of the frozen D09 family/partition specifications
    (contract §15 challenge matrix + partition builder definitions,
    2026-08-14).
  * Disposition is DERIVED by the contract rule engine (contract §8/§9)
    exclusively from contract-authorized input facts carried in the spec
    rows: coverage (L0/L1/accepted_current), source revisions and declared
    content hashes, stratum admission, cutoff identity state, counterevidence
    declared/matched rule refs, denominator/opportunity state, member
    origins/cutoff relations/public identities, gap visit/time anchors,
    member locators, visibility rate state and the locatable
    ModeContract design-clause ref. There are NO semantic tags, skips or
    hardcoded dispositions/counts in the oracle: every decisive fact also
    exists in the catalog typed_input (contract-authorized), so an independent
    verifier can re-derive all 179 dispositions and decisive counts from the
    catalog alone with zero skips.
  * Expected/trace/source leaves are computed only here.
  * Standard library only. No network, no wall-clock, no randomness.
  * Deterministic: two fresh generations are byte-identical (canonical UTF-8,
    NFC, no-whitespace JSON, sorted keys, stable ordering, SHA-256).

Design decisions (documented for the independent verifier):
  D1. One D09 pattern unit per admitted ownable case; zero units for
      consume-only / routing-gate / global-admission-failed / trend-gate
      cases. Zero-unit cases carry case-level disposition not_applicable.
  D2. Numerator semantics: repeated_subject_risk -> unique in-cutoff
      subjects/events from spec member rows; members with
      origin_decision=verified_same_origin are deduped by
      (public_r4_risk_identity, subject_stable_id) per contract §5.2 (the
      dedup groups are input facts, e.g. CASE-047's two D02+D08 pairs);
      systematic_data_or_process_gap -> accepted gap members (each member is
      one missing opportunity); within_site_time_trend -> change-ledger
      subjects. Non-positive/non-boundary units report numerator zero.
  D3. measure.opportunity_missing = expected - observed (the catalog
      envelope's missing_opportunity_refs are not authoritative for these
      synthetic cases; the spec semantics are).
  D4. risk_count=1 iff positive; clue_count=1 iff boundary; query_count=1
      iff positive and the resolved Query redundancy decision allows it and
      the resolvable member list stays within the resolved fanout limit.
  D5. Lineage: handoff iff positive or carry_forward; superseded iff
      rule_supersession / window_definition_change.
  D6. Stable core serialization:
      project_ref|site|pattern_definition_id|analysis_window_stable_id|
      stratum_contract_id|stratum_key (contract §5.1); trend uses the
      current (last) window stable id.
  D7. Canonical JSON and hashing conventions identical to D07/D08/worker_01:
      Unicode NFC, sorted object keys, no whitespace, ensure_ascii=False,
      SHA-256 content hash over all keys except content_hash.
  D8. Derived decision levels (counterevidence level, deep-link deficiency,
      integrity blocks, visibility boundary) are FUNCTIONS of the spec facts
      above; the synthetic naming conventions (member id -> default public
      identity; revision -> declared content hash convention)
      are documented and mirrored by the catalog generator so both sides
      derive identical facts independently.
"""

